<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zela</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zile</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zela was an ancient city of Pontus in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, now Zile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokat">Tokat</a> Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, built around a temple-state of the goddess Anaitis. Two battles were fought there: in 67 BCE Mithridates VI destroyed a Roman army under Triarius, and in 47 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharnaces-ii-of-pontus">Pharnaces II</a> so quickly that he reported 'veni, vidi, vici'.</p></div>
